{"model": "gpt-6-luna", "qid": "q003", "dataset": "sat_math", "para": 3, "sample": "g", "temp": 0.0, "answer": "C", "correct": true, "content_len": 710, "reasoning_len": 0, "snippet": "The equation $y = 0.56x + 27.2$ is in slope-intercept form $y = mx + b$, where $m = 0.56$ is the slope.\n\nThe slope represents the rate of change: for each 1-unit increase in $x$ (each additional year), $y$ increases by 0.56. Since $y$ is the average number of students per classroom, 0.56 represents the estimated annual increase in the average number of students per classroom.\n\n- Option (A): The total number of students in 2000 — incorrect.\n- Option (B): The average in 2000 is $y$ when $x = 0$, i.e., 27.2 — incorrect.\n- Option (C): The estimated increase each year — correct, matches the slope.\n- Option (D): The difference in 2010 vs 2000 would be $0.56 \\times 10 = 5.6$, not 0.56 — incorrect.\n\nAnswer: C", "usage": {"pt": 495, "ct": 238}, "t": 1792301108.6}
