{"model": "gpt-6-luna", "qid": "q005", "dataset": "sat_math", "para": 2, "sample": "g", "temp": 0.0, "answer": "A", "correct": true, "content_len": 237, "reasoning_len": 0, "snippet": "Since $(0,0)$ is a solution to the system:\n\nSubstitute $x = 0$, $y = 0$ into both inequalities:\n\n1. $y < -x + a \\Rightarrow 0 < a$\n2. $y > x + b \\Rightarrow 0 > b \\Rightarrow b < 0$\n\nSo $a > 0$ and $b < 0$. This means $a > b$.\n\nAnswer: A", "usage": {"pt": 430, "ct": 98}, "t": 1792301370.8}
{"model": "gpt-6-luna", "qid": "q005", "dataset": "sat_math", "para": 3, "sample": "g", "temp": 0.0, "answer": "A", "correct": true, "content_len": 352, "reasoning_len": 0, "snippet": "Since $(0,0)$ is a solution to the system of inequalities:\n\nSubstitute $x = 0$ and $y = 0$ into both inequalities:\n\n1. $y < -x + a \\Rightarrow 0 < 0 + a \\Rightarrow a > 0$\n2. $y > x + b \\Rightarrow 0 > 0 + b \\Rightarrow b < 0$\n\nFrom (1): $a > 0$, so $a$ is positive.\nFrom (2): $b < 0$, so $b$ is negative.\n\nTherefore, $a > b$ must be true.\n\nAnswer: (A)", "usage": {"pt": 422, "ct": 141}, "t": 1792301397.4}
{"model": "gpt-6-luna", "qid": "q005", "dataset": "sat_math", "para": 4, "sample": "g", "temp": 0.0, "answer": "A", "correct": true, "content_len": 3, "reasoning_len": 0, "snippet": "(A)", "usage": {"pt": 425, "ct": 3}, "t": 1792301404.4}
{"model": "gpt-6-luna", "qid": "q005", "dataset": "sat_math", "para": 5, "sample": "g", "temp": 0.0, "answer": "A", "correct": true, "content_len": 151, "reasoning_len": 0, "snippet": "Substitute $(0,0)$:\n1. $0 < 0 + a \\Rightarrow a > 0$\n2. $0 > 0 + b \\Rightarrow b < 0$\n\nSince $a$ is positive and $b$ is negative, $a > b$.\n\nAnswer: (A)", "usage": {"pt": 426, "ct": 68}, "t": 1792301424.6}
{"model": "gpt-6-luna", "qid": "q005", "dataset": "sat_math", "para": 6, "sample": "g", "temp": 0.0, "answer": "A", "correct": true, "content_len": 182, "reasoning_len": 0, "snippet": "Since $(0,0)$ is a solution, substitute $x=0$, $y=0$:\n\n$0 < 0 + a \\Rightarrow a > 0$\n$0 > 0 + b \\Rightarrow b < 0$\n\nThus $a$ is positive and $b$ is negative, so $a > b$.\n\nAnswer: (A)", "usage": {"pt": 425, "ct": 78}, "t": 1792301438.2}
{"model": "gpt-6-luna", "qid": "q006", "dataset": "gsm8k", "para": 1, "sample": "g", "temp": 0.0, "answer": "4", "correct": false, "content_len": 2384, "reasoning_len": 0, "snippet": "Step 1: Total days recorded over the past month = 30.\n\nStep  ... ? That's 4.\n\nThe next three days info seems like a distractor, since they're after the month.\n\nSo the answer: 4 good days were left in the month (after the first 24 days).\n\nLet me reconsider the phrasing: \"Christina records her mood every day on a calendar. Over the past thirty days of moods...\" So the month = 30 days. \"If the next three days were good, neutral, and good, how many good days were left in the month?\"\n\nThe \"next three days\" are after the 30-day month, so they don't affect \"in the month.\" The month has 12 good days total. First 8 days good. Remaining days in month = 6, among which good days left = 12 − 8 = 4.\n\nAnswer: 4", "usage": {"pt": 407, "ct": 711}, "t": 1792301612.5}
