{"model": "gpt-6-luna", "qid": "q006", "dataset": "gsm8k", "para": 5, "sample": "g", "temp": 0.0, "answer": "8", "correct": false, "content_len": 689, "reasoning_len": 0, "snippet": "Let me work through this step by step.\n\nThe 30-day period is divided into three chunks of 8 days each:\n- First 8 days: all good (8 good days)\n- Second 8 days: all bad (0 good days)\n- Third 8 days: all neutral (0 good days)\n\nSo far: 8 good days, 16 of the 30 days accounted for. Remaining: 14 days.\n\nThe next 3 days (days 17, 18, 19) are: good, neutral, good\n- That adds 2 more good days\n\nGood days so far: 8 + 2 = 10 good days out of 19 days.\n\nRemaining days in the month: 30 - 19 = 11 days, none of which are specified as good.\n\nSo the total good days = 8 + 2 = 10.\n\nGood days left in the month (after the next three days): 10 total - 2 already counted in those three days = 8.\n\nAnswer: 8", "usage": {"pt": 411, "ct": 239}, "t": 1792301700.6}
